,title,link,text,language,family
0,"Manobo, Agusan Language (MSM)... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/msm/,"Agusan Manobo is a stable indigenous language of the Philippines. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Manobo, Agusan",Austronesian
1,Agusan Manobo – TIPs,https://tips.translation.bible/tip_language/msm/,"Agusan Manobo (msm) is a(n) Austronesian language of Philippines, marked as not endangered.The Greek that is translated as “carried by four of them” in English had to be translated as “four men carried him slung between two poles in a hammock” in Agusan Manobo.","Manobo, Agusan",Austronesian
2,Manobo (Agusan) Language Sample | Language Museum,https://www.language-museum.com/encyclopedia/m/manobo-agusan.php,"If you want to get a flavour of the Manobo (Agusan) language, check out a small sample at the Language Museum.Philippines (40,000) - Total (40,000). Classification. Austronesian | Malayo-Polynesian.","Manobo, Agusan",Austronesian
3,"Manobo, Agusan (MSM) - Download the Free Bible App. Download...",https://www.bible.com/te/versions/979-msm-manobo-agusan,"Manobo, Agusan (MSM) - Hundreds of versions in 1600+ different languages - the Bible that goes with you anywhere. Download now or read online.","Manobo, Agusan",Austronesian
4,"Manobo, Umayamnon in Philippines people group... | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/18945/rp,"Learn about the Manobo, Umayamnon in Philippines people group.Their existence and survival are being threatened in their ancestral domain by the migrants and some other sub-tribes of Bukidnon and Agusan del Sur. Besides, they need appropriate livelihood projects for daily needs.","Manobo, Agusan",Austronesian
5,"Manobo, Agusan",https://www.tbsbibles.org/page/language-msm,"60,000speakers. The Manobo or Manubu languages, spoken by various indigenous groups in Mindanao, Philippines, belong to the Austronesian language family. Agusan Manobo, spoken in northeastern Mindanao is a standard form for the various languages.","Manobo, Agusan",Austronesian
6,"Manobo, Agusan: Omayamnon language. Evangelism tools, church...",https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/26130,"Manobo, Agusan: Omayamnon language and dialect information. Audio Bible stories and lessons. Download free evangelism resources, MP3s, audio bible study tools, language/dialect information.","Manobo, Agusan",Austronesian
7,The World of Agusan Manobo Music,https://jacklegpreacher.com/filipinoharp/manobo/Philippine_Music_at_the_Frontiers/Ritual_Acts_in_Curing_Ritual.html,"Manobo elaborate rituals have two parts. In both, the possessed medium dances, in trance, to the rhythms of the paired drum and gong.","Manobo, Agusan",Austronesian
8,PAMANA:Kahusayan at Tagumpay sa Edukasyon (Featuring: Agusan...),https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1uqrk6UKJEo,A DepEd Caraga Region Entry to the Cultural Dance Contes-National Level...,"Manobo, Agusan",Austronesian
9,Ethnic Groups of Mindanao - Philippine Indigenous | PPTX,https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/ethnic-groups-of-mindanao-philippine-indigenous/287465006,Language or Dialect •Speak Manobo languages (Austronesian family) • Different dialects by area: – Agusan Manobo – Bukidnon Manobo – Cotabato Manobo – Ata-Manobo • Many also speak Cebuano and Filipino MANOBO. 6.,"Manobo, Agusan",Austronesian
